          "evidence": "PART-07 and PART-08 can publish prior state from In(local_state) to PART-06 and separately publish unwrapped post-transition state to eligibility/composition. Trusted Isolette demonstrates local state, initialization, compute cases, and In(state); the accepted factory-medium source demonstrates simultaneous pre-state context and post-state publication, so the feedback paths are state-broken without another owner or interaction.",
          "requested_change": ""
        },
        {
          "classification": "no-concern",
          "evidence": "Extensional audit found nonidentity facts at every claimed usage: PART-01..03 have many-to-one presence/usability/event classifications; PART-04..05 add multi-field qualification/readiness; PART-06..09 make state-dependent coherence and lifecycle/recovery transitions; PART-10..12 combine multiple inputs into proposals; PART-13 applies strict priority; and PART-14 derives a recovery-dominant mode that collapses both release actions. Copied tags, fields, states, decisions, and dispositions are explicitly uncredited.",
          "requested_change": ""
        },
        {
          "classification": "no-concern",
          "evidence": "The bounded product is exactly 3,240 root snapshots times 30 prior-state tuples, or 97,200 evaluations. Separate PART-01..14 candidate evaluators can exchange only INT values and be compared with an uncredited independently written abstract reference relation, including intermediate-value, 29-case, priority, composition, and ten-scenario checks. The harness independently typechecks, binds the source hash, rejects analyzer gaps/overlaps/mismatches or failed checks, and requires matching passed ownership records.",
          "requested_change": ""
        }
      ]
